            "tests": [
                {
                    "id": "typical_midday_all_outputs",
                    "description": "Anchor test at the upstream typical-midday scenario (NO=2.5e16 ~1 ppb, NO2=5.0e16 ~2 ppb, O3=1.0e18 ~40 ppb, O2=5.25e24, M=2.5e25 — test/test_nox_photochemistry.jl:59-63). Reproduces and tightens two upstream testitems at once: `Eq 6.5 O Atom Steady-State` (asserts 0 < O < 1.0e12 — here O = 5.08e9, well inside the band) and `Eq 6.6 Leighton Relationship` (asserts 1e17 < O3_pss < 1e19 and O3_pss ≈ 8.42e17 at rtol=0.05 — here O3_pss pinned exactly at 8.421052631578948e17). All four outputs are pinned at rel=1e-10. Note O3_pss = 8.42e17 < O3 = 1.0e18, so Φ = 0.842 < 1 and P_O3 < 0 — the default ambient ozone sits above its photostationary value.",
                    "parameter_overrides": {},
                    "time_span": {
                        "start": 0.0,
                        "end": 1.0
                    },
                    "assertions": [
                        {
                            "variable": "O",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 5079365079.365079
                        },
                        {
                            "variable": "O3_pss",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 8.421052631578948e+17
                        },
                        {
                            "variable": "Φ",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 0.8421052631578947
                        },
                        {
                            "variable": "P_O3",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": -75000000000000.0
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "phi_unity_at_photostationary_state",
                    "description": "Reproduces the upstream `Eq 6.7 Photostationary State Parameter` and `Eq 6.8 Net O3 Production` at-PSS cases (test/test_nox_photochemistry.jl:127-137, 164-173). The ambient O3 is overridden to the photostationary value O3_pss = j_NO2·NO2/(k_NO_O3·NO) = 8.421052631578948e17 m⁻³ computed at the default NO/NO2. At exact photostationary state Φ = O3_pss/O3 = 1.0 and the net ozone production P_O3 = j_NO2·NO2 − k_NO_O3·NO·O3 = 0.0 (the source exactly balances the sink). The upstream asserts Φ ≈ 1.0 at rtol=1e-6 and |P_O3|/(j_NO2·NO2) < 1e-6; this test pins Φ = 1.0 exactly and P_O3 = 0.0 with an abs tolerance of 1.0 (the IEEE-754 near-cancellation residual is sub-ULP — far below the upstream's 4e8 'effectively zero' threshold).",
                    "parameter_overrides": {
                        "O3": 8.421052631578948e+17
                    },
                    "time_span": {
                        "start": 0.0,
                        "end": 1.0
                    },
                    "assertions": [
                        {
                            "variable": "Φ",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 1.0
                        },
                        {
                            "variable": "P_O3",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 0.0,
                            "tolerance": {
                                "abs": 1.0
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "phi_above_unity_below_pss",
                    "description": "Reproduces the upstream `Eq 6.7`/`Eq 6.8` below-PSS cases (test/test_nox_photochemistry.jl:140-142, 176-178). The ambient O3 is overridden to half the photostationary value (0.5·O3_pss = 4.210526315789474e17 m⁻³). Below photostationary state the NO₂-photolysis source outruns the NO+O₃ sink: Φ = O3_pss/O3 = 2.0 > 1 (the upstream asserts Φ > 1) and the net ozone production P_O3 = +2.0e14 m⁻³/s > 0 (the upstream asserts P_O3 > 0). Physically this is the regime where peroxy-radical chemistry would be driving ozone formation. Both outputs pinned at rel=1e-10.",
                    "parameter_overrides": {
                        "O3": 4.210526315789474e+17
                    },
                    "time_span": {
                        "start": 0.0,
                        "end": 1.0
                    },
                    "assertions": [
                        {
                            "variable": "Φ",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 2.0
                        },
                        {
                            "variable": "P_O3",
                            "time": 0.0,
                            "expected": 200000000000000.0
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "phi_below_unity_above_pss",
                    "description": "Reproduces the upstream `Eq 6.7`/`Eq 6.8` above-PSS cases (test/test_nox_photochemistry.jl:145-147, 181-183). The ambient O3 is overridden to twice the photostationary value (2.0·O3_pss = 1.6842105263157896e18 m⁻³). Above photostationary state the NO+O₃ sink outruns the NO₂-photolysis source: Φ = O3_pss/O3 = 0.5 < 1 (the upstream asserts Φ < 1) and the net ozone production P_O3 = -4.0e14 m⁻³/s < 0 (the upstream asserts P_O3 < 0) — net ozone loss. Both outputs pinned at rel=1e-10.",
                    "parameter_overrides": {
                        "O3": 1.6842105263157896e+18
