                {
                    "id": "o_atom_linear_in_j_no2",
                    "description": "Exercises Eq. 6.5's linear dependence of the O-atom steady state on the photolysis rate. With j_NO2 doubled to 1.6e-2 s⁻¹ (all concentrations at their typical-midday defaults), O = j_NO2·NO2/(k_O_O2_M·O2·M) = 10158730158.730158 m⁻³ — exactly 2× the default O of 5079365079.365079. Pinned at rel=1e-10. Confirms the O atom tracks the instantaneous NO₂ photolysis rate, the basis of the quasi-steady-state assumption underlying Eq. 6.5.",
                    "parameter_overrides": {
                        "j_NO2": 0.016
                    },
                    "time_span": {
                        "start": 0.0,
                        "end": 1.0
