                            "expected": 10158730158.730158
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "o_atom_inverse_in_air_density",
                    "description": "Exercises Eq. 6.5's inverse dependence of the O-atom steady state on the total air number density M (the third body in O + O₂ + M → O₃). With M doubled to 5.0e25 m⁻³ (all other inputs at their typical-midday defaults), the O-atom quenching denominator doubles, so O = 2539682539.6825395 m⁻³ — exactly half the default O of 5079365079.365079. Pinned at rel=1e-10. Physically this is why the ground-state O atom is more abundant per unit photolysis at high altitude (low M): the recombination sink weakens faster than the source.",
                    "parameter_overrides": {
                        "M": 5e+25
                    },
                    "time_span": {
                        "start": 0.0,
                        "end": 1.0
                    },
                    "assertions": [
