                            "expected": 2539682539.6825395
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "id": "polluted_urban_high_nox",
                    "description": "Polluted-urban regime: NO=2.5e17 m⁻³ (~10 ppb), NO2=7.5e17 m⁻³ (~30 ppb), O3=2.5e18 m⁻³ (~100 ppb), O2/M at defaults. Exercises all four outputs at the high-NOx end of the tropospheric range. O3_pss = 1.2631578947368422e18 m⁻³ (~50 ppb — the photostationary value implied by the NO2/NO = 3 ratio). The ambient O3 of 100 ppb sits well above O3_pss, so Φ = 0.505 < 1 and P_O3 = -5.875e15 m⁻³/s < 0 (strong net ozone loss by the pure cycle — in reality offset by the peroxy-radical production this component omits). O = 7.62e10 m⁻³. All pinned at rel=1e-10.",
